        "titulo": "The prepositions of the genitive",
        "explicacao": "The prepositions of the genitive. Now the prepositions that take the genitive. These are the most important. I will explain each with examples. БЕЗ: without. Notice: the object after без goes into the genitive. ДЛЯ: for. Notice: the object after для goes into the genitive. ДО: until, before. ИЗ: from (origin). Notice: из shows origin, where something comes out of. Do not confuse it with от, which shows moving away from a person. ОТ: from (moving away). Notice: от is used with people (moving away from them). Из is used with places (origin). У: at, by, at someone's place. Notice: у is already familiar from the \"have\" sentences (у меня́ есть). Here it means \"by\" or \"at someone's place\". О́КОЛО: near. КРО́МЕ: except. ПО́СЛЕ: after.",
